              "@id": "urn:uuid:1204d70e-6d98-53d8-b363-d3928f82ffd7",
              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "BRYAN SCHRODER\nUnited States Attorney\n\nKYLE REARDON\nANNE J. VELDHUIS\nAssistant U.S. Attorneys\nFederal Building & U.S. Courthouse\n222 West Seventh Avenue, #9, Room 253\nAnchorage, Alaska 99513-7567\nPhone: (907) 271-5071\nFax: (907) 271-1500\nEmail: kyle.reardon@usdoj.gov\nanne.veldhuis@usdoj.gov\n\nAttorneys for Plaintiff\n\nIN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n\nFOR THE DISTRICT OF ALASKA\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA, ) No. 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS\n)\nPlaintiff, ) COUNT 1:\n) CONSPIRACY TO ENGAGE IN SEX\nv. ) TRAFFICKING OF MINORS\n) Vio. of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1594(c)\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a )\n\u201cGoo,\u201d ) COUNTS 2 \u2013 5:\n) SEX TRAFFICKING OF A MINOR\nDefendant. ) Vio. of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1591\n)\n) COUNTS 6 - 8:\n) SEXUAL EXPLOITATION OF A\n) CHILD \u2013 PRODUCTION OF CHILD\n) PORNOGRAPHY\n) Vio. of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a), (e)\n)\n) COUNTS 9 - 10:\n) FELON IN POSSESSION OF\n) FIREARM AND AMMUNITION\n) Vio. of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 922(g)(1) and\n) 924(a)(2)\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 1 of 18\n) CRIMINAL FORFEITURE\n) ALLEGATION 1\n) 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 924(d) and\n) 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2461(c)\n)\n) CRIMINAL FORFEITURE\n) ALLEGATION 2\n) 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2253 and\n) 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2461(c)\n)\n\nFOURTH SUPERSEDING INDICTMENT\n\nThe Grand Jury charges that:\n\nCOUNT 1\n\nIntroduction\n\nAt all times relevant to this indictment:\n\n1. Defendant TRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d was a convicted\n\nfelon, with prior convictions for attempted robbery, drug possession, assault, and\n\npossession of crack cocaine with the intent to distribute. Among other ventures, GRANT\n\nclaimed to be the owner of a commercial pornography business called \u201cHU$H.\u201d GRANT\n\nlived in multiple locations in Anchorage, Alaska.\n\n2. COCONSPIRATOR 1 was a resident of Anchorage, Alaska, living in an\n\napartment that she shared at various times with her mother, sisters, and GRANT.\n\n3. \u201cJ.S.,\u201d a minor female born in 2001, was a resident of the District of\n\nAlaska. COCONSPIRATOR 1 has known \u201cJ.S.\u201d since at least 2015. \u201cJ.S.\u201d met GRANT\n\nPage 2 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 2 of 18\nin September or October 2018, and told him her age upon meeting him or shortly\n\nthereafter.\n\n4. \u201cK.C.,\u201d a minor female born in 2003, was a resident of the District of\n\nAlaska. \u201cJ.S.\u201d introduced \u201cK.C.\u201d to GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 in October or\n\nNovember 2018. GRANT learned her age shortly after her arrival.\n\n5. A \u201ccommercial sex act\u201d is any sex act, on account of which anything of\n\nvalue is given to or received by any person.\n\n6. Prostitutes are persons who engage in commercial sex acts. Individuals\n\nwho through various means of coercion, including enticement, intimidation, or force,\n\nenlist individuals to become prostitutes, and who profit from the prostitution of others are\n\ncalled \"pimps.\u201d Pimps are sometimes euphemistically referred to as \"management.\u201d\n\nPimps can be either male or female. In addition, pimps can sometimes work in\n\npartnership with other pimps.\n\n7. Pimps and prostitutes have embraced the internet as a means of advertising\n\nservices and communicating with customers. Certain web sites have been created to\n\nfacilitate communications between prostitutes and their clients, and to allow pimps and\n\nprostitutes to communicate services and prices to potential customers. One website used\n\nfor such purposes is Adultlook.com. These advertisements also generally include a\n\nphone number for the customer to contact if they are interested in engaging in a\n\ncommercial sex act. Often, photographs of the prostitutes are posted along with the\n\nadvertisements. These photographs often show the prostitutes posed provocatively in\n\nPage 3 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 3 of 18\nvarious states of undress. User profiles and advertisements can be created on a computer;\n\nhowever, most advertisements are created and posted using internet-enabled smart\n\nphones.\n\n8. In addition to using them to create and post advertisements, pimps and\n\nprostitutes use cell phones in order to communicate directly with potential customers.\n\nThrough the phone numbers included in the online advertisements, customers contact\n\npimps or prostitutes in order to negotiate the terms and conditions of a commercial sex\n\nact. Contact is made through phone calls as well as text messages. These terms and\n\nconditions, can include price, the service to be provided, and the location. Locations can\n\ninclude \u201cin-calls,\u201d meaning commercial sex acts where the customer travels to the\n\nprostitute\u2019s location; \u201cout-calls,\u201d meaning commercial sex acts where the prostitute\n\ntravels to the customer\u2019s location, and \u201ccar dates,\u201d meaning commercial sex acts that take\n\nplace in one of the parties\u2019 vehicles. \u201cIn-calls\u201d and \u201cout-calls\u201d may take place in either\n\nparties\u2019 residence, or may occur in a hotel or motel room that one of the parties has\n\nrented.\n\n9. Cell phones are also used by pimps and the prostitutes who work for them\n\nin order to communicate with each other.\n\n10. Most juvenile prostitutes have pimps, who provide instructions to the\n\nprostitutes. These instructions include when to work, what to wear, how to speak with\n\ncustomers, and what prices to charge. Pimps also provide varying levels of support to the\n\nprostitutes who work for them, to include food, shelter, clothing, and transportation. In\n\nPage 4 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 4 of 18\nsome cases, pimps will also provide drugs to the prostitutes who work for them. These\n\ndrugs are provided for multiple reasons, to include feeding the prostitute\u2019s addiction,\n\nproviding them with the energy to continue working, as an inducement to motivate the\n\nprostitute to continue working, or some combination of the above. In exchange, pimps\n\nreceive some or all of the money that a prostitute makes from the commercial sex acts\n\nthat he or she engages in with customers, or receives items the prostitute buys with the\n\nmoney earned from these commercial sex acts.\n\n11. In addition to the use of drugs, pimps at times use multiple other means to\n\ncontrol the actions of the prostitutes who work for them, including physical force, the\n\nthreat of physical force, and fear. Force can be direct through hitting, punching, slapping,\n\nor beating a prostitute. It can also be indirect. Indirect threats can include being warned\n\nby the pimp about harm that may result if the prostitute disobeys a pimp\u2019s orders,\n\nwitnessing others being physically assaulted, or being told by the pimp or others about\n\nviolence committed against other victims. Force can also include sexual assault or the\n\nthreat of sexual assault. Pimps may also use coercive means other than physical harm or\n\nthe threat of physical harm to control the prostitutes who work for them. These non-\n\nviolent coercive means include the threat of homelessness, sextortion or the threat of\n\npublication to the community of the prostitute\u2019s actions, threats to abuse legal process, or\n\nthreats to prevent or limit a prostitute\u2019s access to a child. Pimps also use displays of\n\naffection in order to manipulate prostitutes. Most pimps employ some combination of all\n\nof the above to effectively manage the prostitutes who work for them.\n\nPage 5 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 5 of 18\n12. Pimps often possess firearms to assist in protecting and intimidating their\n\nprostitutes.\n\nManner and Means\n\n13. The purpose of the conspiracy was to obtain money and other items of\n\nvalue for GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1.\n\n14. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 harbored homeless and transient\n\nminors by allowing them to stay at COCONSPIRATOR 1\u2019s residence in Anchorage,\n\nAlaska, and providing for them and maintaining them while they were at the residence.\n\n15. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 recruited, enticed, and coerced those\n\nhomeless minor victims to engage in commercial sex acts.\n\n16. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 worked with the minors to create and\n\npost online advertisements on Adultlook.com. Customers responded to these\n\nadvertisements, and GRANT, COCONSPIRATOR 1, and the minor victims\n\ncommunicated through phone calls and text messages with potential commercial sex\n\ncustomers.\n\n17. COCONSPIRATOR 1 provided instructions to \u201cK.C.\u201d about how to work\n\nas a prostitute, including directing her on how much to charge for various sex acts, and\n\ninstructing her to refer to the money customers would pay her as \u201croses.\u201d\n\n18. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 instructed \u201cK.C.\u201d to use her status as a\n\nminor to blackmail customers at the conclusion of commercial sex acts.\n\nPage 6 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 6 of 18\n19. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 coordinated with customers, the minor\n\nvictims, and each other for \u201cin-calls\u201d to occur in COCONSPIRATOR 1\u2019s apartment.\n\nGRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 transported the minor victims to meet customers in\n\norder to have the minor victims engage in \u201cout calls\u201d and \u201ccar dates.\u201d These commercial\n\nsex acts occurred in and around Anchorage, Alaska.\n\n20. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 used various and multiple means to\n\ncoerce and entice the minor victims to engage in commercial sex acts. GRANT used\n\nphysical force, threats of force, drugs, and brandished firearms in order to coerce and\n\nentice the minor victims. COCONSPIRATOR 1 used force, threats of force, drugs,\n\nthreats of homelessness, and brandished firearms in order to coerce and entice the minor\n\nvictims.\n\nActs in Furtherance of the Conspiracy\n\n21. In or about mid-October 2018, COCONSPIRATOR 1 communicated with a\n\ncommercial sex customer who specifically wanted to have sex with a minor.\n\nCOCONSPIRATOR 1 provided \u201cJ.S.\u201d to the customer for this date. Upon completion of\n\nthe commercial sex act, the customer provided money to \u201cJ.S.\u201d COCONSPIRATOR 1\n\nthen took the money and kept it.\n\n22. On at least one occasion, GRANT coordinated directly with a customer to\n\narrange a commercial sex act for \u201cJ.S.\u201d The customer paid $300 for the commercial sex\n\nact. \u201cJ.S.\u201d gave the money to GRANT.\n\nPage 7 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 7 of 18\n23. On at least one occasion, GRANT drove \u201cJ.S.\u201d to meet a customer for a\n\ncommercial sex act and waited outside for the commercial sex act to conclude.\n\n24. On at least one occasion, GRANT and \u201cJ.S.\u201d got into a car with GRANT\u2019s\n\nassociates. Upon entering the car, GRANT ordered \u201cJ.S.\u201d not to have sex with any of the\n\nassociates unless they paid her first.\n\n25. \u201cJ.S.\u201d used money that she earned through commercial sex acts to buy\n\nclothing for GRANT from Foot Locker.\n\n26. On one occasion, COCONSPIRATOR 1 drove \u201cJ.S.\u201d to meet a customer\n\nfor a commercial sex act. At the conclusion of the act, the customer paid \u201cJ.S.\u201d\n\nCOCONSPIRATOR 1 took this money and kept it. COCONSPIRATOR 1 then\n\nconfronted the customer and demanded additional payment from the customer, telling\n\nhim that she knew that he was in the military, and that she could get him in trouble for\n\n\u201cfucking a minor.\u201d\n\n27. On October 22, 2018, COCONSPIRATOR 1 sent a text message to a\n\ncustomer telling him she wants her \u201cfucking cash upfront,\u201d and threatening to post video\n\nfootage of the customer having sex with a minor prostitute if he did not pay.\n\n28. GRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 assisted \u201cK.C.\u201d with the creation of an\n\nonline profile for a prostitution-related website. \u201cK.C.\u201d used COCONSPIRATOR 1\u2019s\n\ncell phone to create this advertisement. This advertisement used the moniker \u201cLady\n\nSilky,\u201d and was used by GRANT, COCONSPIRATOR 1, and \u201cK.C.\u201d to advertise \u201cK.C.\u201d\n\nfor commercial sex acts, and to communicate with customers.\n\nPage 8 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 8 of 18\n29. On one occasion, COCONSPIRATOR 1 drove \u201cK.C.\u201d to meet a customer\n\nfor a \u201ccar date.\u201d \u201cJ.S.\u201d traveled with COCONSPIRATOR 1 and \u201cK.C.\u201d During the\n\ncommercial sex act, COCONSPIRATOR 1 possessed a firearm, and after approximately\n\n20 minutes COCONSPIRATOR 1 banged on the car door and told the customer it was\n\n\u201ctime to go.\u201d The customer then went to an ATM in order to get money to pay \u201cK.C.\u201d\n\nAt the ATM, COCONSPIRATOR 1 informed the customer that he had just had sex with\n\na minor, that she had filmed it, and that he would therefore have to pay more than the\n\npreviously negotiated price.\n\n30. On October 30, 2018, between 12:26 a.m. and 12:27 a.m., GRANT and\n\nCOCONSPIRATOR 1 exchanged the following text messages related to \u201cK.C.:\u201d\n\na. GRANT: Yo we get frm over here and silky need to go home how\n\nyou done try and leave her out here wit this messy bitch\n\n[REDACTED] she trying to snatch shorty fro crazy if I gotta spend\n\nbread to get a room I\u2019m not fucking wit you until you pay a fee facts\n\nb. COCONSPIRATOR 1: Keep her with u we coming\n\n31. On October 30, 2018, between 11:59 a.m. and 12:15 p.m.\n\nCOCONSPIRATOR 1 and GRANT exchanged the following text messages related to\n\n\u201cK.C.:\u201d\n\na. COCONSPIRATOR 1: Stop givin that fucking girl pills I don\u2019t need\n\nher passing out n u ain\u2019t watching her tf weird\n\nPage 9 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 9 of 18\nb. GRANT: What I gave her a zany that they gave me last night and\n\ndnt be checking me bout nothing tf and I\u2019m at the doctor wit my\n\nbaby what are you doing\n\nc. GRANT: Are you catching a fucking cab cause it just hit my phone\n\nd. COCONSPIRATOR 1: That\u2019s beside the point I don\u2019t need this\n\nbitch passing out in public with me tf nigga u don\u2019t give me zans\n\nnun so wtf is ya problem with her nigga she younger then me an yea\n\nthat\u2019s coo stop giving her shit period\n\n32. During the time that \u201cJ.S.\u201d resided at COCONSPIRATOR 1\u2019s apartment,\n\nGRANT and COCONSPIRATOR 1 made at least three sexually explicit videos involving\n\nthe minor victim. At least one of the videos was branded with the \u201cHU$H\u201d logo.\n\nThe Conspiracy\n\n33. Between a date unknown to the Grand Jury, and no later than on or about\n\nDecember 1, 2018, in the District of Alaska, in and affecting interstate commerce, the\n\ndefendant, TRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a/ \u201cGoo,\u201d and COCONSPIRATOR 1, did\n\ncombine, conspire, confederate, and agree with each other, to knowingly recruit, entice,\n\nharbor, transport, provide, obtain, and maintain a person, including \u201cJ.S.,\u201d and \u201cK.C.,\u201d\n\na/k/a \u201cSilky,\u201d having had a reasonable opportunity to observe the person, and knowing\n\nand in reckless disregard that the person had not attained the age of 18 years old, and\n\nwould be caused to engage in a commercial sex act, in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1591.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1594(c).\n\nPage 10 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 10 of 18\nCOUNT 2\n\n34. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n35. Between a date unknown to the Grand Jury, and on or about December 1,\n\n2018, in the District of Alaska, in and affecting interstate commerce, the defendant,\n\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a/ \u201cGoo,\u201d did knowingly recruit, entice, harbor,\n\ntransport, provide, obtain, advertise, and maintain by any means, a person, to wit: \u201cJ.S.,\u201d\n\nhaving had a reasonable opportunity to observe the person, and knowing and in reckless\n\ndisregard that the person had not attained the age of 18 years old, and would be caused to\n\nengage in a commercial sex act.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1591(a)(1).\n\nCOUNT 3\n\n36. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n37. Between a date unknown to the Grand Jury, and on or about December 1,\n\n2018, in the District of Alaska, in and affecting interstate commerce, the defendant,\n\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a/ \u201cGoo,\u201d did benefit, financially and by receiving\n\nanything of value, from participating in a venture that has knowingly recruited, enticed,\n\nharbored, transported, provided, obtained, and maintained a person, to wit: \u201cJ.S.,\u201d\n\nknowing and in reckless disregard that the person had not attained the age of 18 years\n\nold, and would be caused to engage in a commercial sex act.\n\nPage 11 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 11 of 18\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1591(a)(2).\n\nCOUNT 4\n\n38. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n39. Between a date unknown to the Grand Jury, and on or about December 1,\n\n2018, in the District of Alaska, in and affecting interstate commerce, the defendant,\n\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a/ \u201cGoo,\u201d did knowingly recruit, entice, harbor,\n\ntransport, provide, obtain, advertise, and maintain by any means, a person, to wit: \u201cK.C.,\u201d\n\na/k/a \u201cSilky,\u201d having had a reasonable opportunity to observe the person, and knowing\n\nand in reckless disregard that the person had not attained the age of 18 years old, and\n\nwould be caused to engage in a commercial sex act.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1591(a)(1).\n\nCOUNT 5\n\n40. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n41. Between a date unknown to the Grand Jury, and on or about December 1,\n\n2018, in the District of Alaska, in and affecting interstate commerce, the defendant,\n\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a/ \u201cGoo,\u201d did benefit, financially and by receiving\n\nanything of value, from participating in a venture that has knowingly recruited, enticed,\n\nharbored, transported, provided, obtained, and maintained a person, to wit: \u201cK.C.,\u201d a/k/a\n\nPage 12 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 12 of 18\n\u201cSilky,\u201d knowing and in reckless disregard that the person had not attained the age of 18\n\nyears old, and would be caused to engage in a commercial sex act.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 1591(a)(2).\n\nCOUNT 6\n\n42. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n43. On or about November 26, 2018, in the District of Alaska, the defendant,\n\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d did employ, use, persuade, induce, entice, and\n\ncoerce a minor, to wit: \u201cJ.S.,\u201d with the intent that such minor engage in sexually explicit\n\nconduct for the purpose of producing a visual depiction of such conduct, knowing that\n\nsuch visual depiction will be transported and transmitted using any means and facility of\n\ninterstate and foreign commerce; was produced using materials that have been mailed,\n\nshipped, and transported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any means,\n\nincluding by computer; and was transported and transmitted using any means and facility\n\nof interstate and foreign commerce, and in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a), (e).\n\nCOUNT 7\n\n44. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n45. On or about November 27, 2018, in the District of Alaska, the defendant,\n\nTRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d did employ, use, persuade, induce, entice, and\n\nPage 13 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 13 of 18\ncoerce a minor, to wit: \u201cJ.S.,\u201d with the intent that such minor engage in sexually explicit\n\nconduct for the purpose of producing a visual depiction of such conduct, knowing that\n\nsuch visual depiction will be transported and transmitted using any means and facility of\n\ninterstate and foreign commerce; was produced using materials that have been mailed,\n\nshipped, and transported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any means,\n\nincluding by computer; and was transported and transmitted using any means and facility\n\nof interstate and foreign commerce, and in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a), (e).\n\nCOUNT 8\n\n46. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n47. On a date unknown to the Grand Jury, but no later than on or about\n\nDecember 12, 2018, in the District of Alaska, the defendant, TRISTAN JAMAL\n\nGRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d did employ, use, persuade, induce, entice, and coerce a minor, to\n\nwit: \u201cJ.S.,\u201d with the intent that such minor engage in sexually explicit conduct for the\n\npurpose of producing a visual depiction of such conduct, knowing that such visual\n\ndepiction will be transported and transmitted using any means and facility of interstate\n\nand foreign commerce; was produced using materials that have been mailed, shipped, and\n\ntransported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any means, including by\n\ncomputer; and was transported and transmitted using any means and facility of interstate\n\nand foreign commerce, and in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce.\n\nPage 14 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 14 of 18\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a) and (e).\n\nCOUNT 9\n\n48. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n49. Between a date unknown to the Grand Jury, but no later than on or about\n\nNovember 15, 2018, and on or about December 13, 2018, within the District of Alaska,\n\nthe defendant, TRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d knowingly having been\n\nconvicted of crimes punishable by imprisonment for a term exceeding one year, did\n\nknowingly possess, in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce, firearms and\n\nammunition, to wit:\n\n1. a Glock 10mm caliber pistol, Model 29GEN4; and\n\n2. 12 rounds of 10mm ammunition.\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2).\n\nCOUNT 10\n\n50. Paragraphs 1 through 32 of this Indictment are re-alleged and incorporated\n\nby reference as if fully set forth herein:\n\n51. Between on or about December 7, 2018, and on or about December 13,\n\n2018, within the District of Alaska, the defendant, TRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a\n\n\u201cGoo,\u201d knowingly having been convicted of crimes punishable by imprisonment for a\n\nterm exceeding one year, did knowingly possess, in and affecting interstate and foreign\n\ncommerce, firearms and ammunition, to wit:\n\nPage 15 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 15 of 18\n1. an IO Inc. 7.62x39 caliber M214 Nano pistol; and\n\n2. 20 rounds of 7.62x39 ammunition.\n\nConvictions\n\nConviction Date Offense Court Case No.\nSpotsylvania\nSale of Drugs on or Circuit Court,\nNovember 7, 2003 177CR0300145200\nnear School Property Spotsylvania\nCounty, Virginia\nSpotsylvania\nCircuit Court,\nAugust 15, 2006 Attempted Robbery 177CR0500159800\nSpotsylvania\nCounty, Virginia\nSuperior Court for\nPossession of a the State of\nAugust 8, 2011 3AN-11-7467\nControlled Substance 4 Alaska, Third\nJudicial District\nSuperior Court for\nthe State of\nMay 21, 2012 Assault 3 3AN-11-10541\nAlaska, Third\nJudicial District\nPossession of a\nFederal District\nControlled Substance\nApril 17, 2013 Court, District of 3:12-cr-00063-SLG\nwith the Intent to\nAlaska\nDistribute\n\nAll of which is in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 922(g)(1) and 924(a)(2).\n\nCRIMINAL FORFEITURE ALLEGATION 1\n\nThe allegations contained in Counts 9 and 10 of this Fourth Superseding\n\nIndictment are hereby re-alleged and incorporated by reference for the purpose of\n\nalleging forfeitures pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 924(d), and 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2461(c).\n\nPage 16 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 16 of 18\nUpon conviction of the offense in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 922(g)(1) and\n\n924(a)(2), as set forth in Counts 11 and 12 of this Fourth Superseding Indictment, the\n\ndefendant, TRISTAN JAMAL GRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d shall forfeit to the United States\n\npursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 924(d) and 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2461(c), any firearm or ammunition\n\ninvolved in or used in knowing violation of the offense, including, but not limited to the\n\nfollowing,\n\n1. a Glock 10mm caliber pistol, Model 29GEN4, serial number BCNA440;\n\n2. 12 rounds of 10mm ammunition;\n\n3. an IO Inc., 7.62x39 caliber M214 Nano pistol, serial number S034347; and\n\n4. 20 rounds of 7.62x39 ammunition.\n\nAll pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 924(d) and 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2461(c), and Rule 32.2(a) of\n\nthe Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure.\n\nCRIMINAL FORFEITURE ALLEGATION 2\n\nThe allegations contained in Counts 6, 7, and 8 are hereby re-alleged and\n\nincorporated by reference for the purpose of alleging forfeitures pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\n\n2253.\n\nUpon conviction of the offenses in violation of 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251 as set forth in\n\nCounts 6, 7, and 8, of this Fourth Superseding Indictment, the defendant, TRISTAN\n\nJAMAL GRANT, a/k/a \u201cGoo,\u201d shall forfeit to the United States pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7\n\n2253 any property, real or personal, that was used or intended to be used to commit or to\n\nfacilitate the commission of such violations, and any property, real or personal,\n\nPage 17 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 17 of 18\nconstituting or derived from, any proceeds obtained, directly or indirectly, as a result of\n\nsuch violations.\n\nAll pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2253 and 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2461(c), and Rule 32.2(a) of the\n\nFederal Rules of Criminal Procedure.\n\nA TRUE BILL.\n\ns/ Grand Jury Foreperson\nGRAND JURY FOREPERSON\n\ns/ Kyle Reardon\nKYLE REARDON\nANNE VELDHUIS\nAssistant U.S. Attorneys\nUnited States of America\n\ns/ Bryan Schroder\nBRYAN SCHRODER\nUnited States Attorney\nUnited States of America\n\nDATE: 11-20-19\n\nPage 18 of 18\n\nCase 3:19-cr-00003-RRB-MMS Document 68 Filed 11/21/19 Page 18 of 18"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
